Appendix B

G‑Rego Formal Syntax and Semantics

B.1 Abstract Syntax

```
Policy     ::= Rule+
Rule       ::= "rule" Identifier "{" Conjunction "}"
Conjunction::= Literal | Literal "AND" Conjunction
Literal    ::= Atom RelOp Atom | TemporalPred "(" Path "," Atom ")"
TemporalPred ::= "EVER" | "NEVER" | "AFTER" "(" Int ")" | "BETWEEN" "(" Int "," Int ")"
Path       ::= Action | Path "ARROW" Action
Atom       ::= Identifier | Number | String
RelOp      ::= "<" | ">" | "<=" | ">=" | "==" | "!="
```

B.2 Denotational Semantics

Let \Sigma be the set of governance states, \mathcal{A} the set of actions, and a trace \tau = a_1 a_2 \dots a_k \in \mathcal{A}^*. The semantics of a Path expression is a sequence of actions that must appear contiguously (not necessarily consecutively) in the trace. We define an interpretation function:

\llbracket \cdot \rrbracket : \text{Policy} \to \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{A}^* \times \Sigma)

For a Rule with conjunction C, a trace \tau and state \sigma satisfy the rule iff for every literal L in C, L holds. We define literal satisfaction:

· Atom1 RelOp Atom2 is a simple comparison over state values.
· EVER(p, a) holds iff the path pattern p occurs somewhere in \tau and when it does, atom a is true.
· NEVER(p, a) holds iff for every occurrence of pattern p, atom a is false.
· AFTER(n)(p, a) holds iff after the first n steps, whenever pattern p occurs, a is true.
· BETWEEN(n,m)(p, a) holds iff for any occurrence of pattern p between step n and m (inclusive), a is true.

The complete evaluation yields a Boolean verdict: \texttt{pass} if the trace-state pair satisfies all rules, \texttt{fail} otherwise. For the LTL_{\text{gov}} fragment, the semantics reduces to monitoring independent safety automata.

B.3 Translation to LTL Safety Automata

Every LTL_{\text{gov}} formula \bigwedge_i \Box(p_i \rightarrow \Box q_i) is transformed into a set of automata as in Chapter 4. The full G‑Rego language can express more complex patterns; the compiler translates these into a combination of simple automata and dynamic programming monitors for the non‑LTL_{\text{gov}} parts.

